  "title": "Permanent DoS in unregisterVault() blocked by 1-wei dust",
  "body": "## Finding description\n```ShareTokenUpgradeable.unregisterVault()``` assumes a vault’s ERC-20 token balance can be made exactly zero and enforces\n```javascript\nif (IERC20(asset).balanceOf(vaultAddress) != 0) {\n    revert CannotUnregisterVaultAssetBalance();\n}\n```\nBecause ERC-20 transfers are permissionless, any external actor can send dust (1 wei) to the vault at any time. In async/pooled vault designs (ERC-7575, rounding, cancellation flows, partial settlements), tiny residuals are common. The strict balance check therefore allows a trivial, permissionless griefing attack\n\n\n## impact\n- Permanent denial-of-service of unregisterVault() for the target vault\n- Permanent consumption of one vault slot protocol may be unable to register new assets (global DoS of multi-asset onboarding).\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nReplace raw balance check with accounting-based validation",
